 "text": "Velcro was invented because of a dog walk. In the 1940s, Swiss engineer Georges de Mestral goes on a walk in the mountains with his dog. They come home covered in burrs, sticky seed pods. He looks at one under a microscope. Tiny hooks, grabbing tiny loops in fabric and fur. So he copies nature. One strip of hooks, one strip of loops. He names it Velcro, from the French words for velvet and hook. Every legend has a beginning.",
